  "priorExpiration": "2002-12-19",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 570.09 Certification of Prescriptions. Certification for specific brand, NHMAC, and FUL drugs, shall conform to the following:\n\n(a) The certification shall be in the licensed practitioner’s own handwriting, or the pharmacist’s own handwriting if a telephone order;\n\n(b) The hand-written certification shall state the term “brand necessary” or “brand medically necessary”;\n\n(c) The certification shall be hand-written directly on the face of the prescription blank; and\n\n(d) Drugs certified as “brand necessary” or “brand medically necessary” shall be subject to prior authorization in accordance with He-W 570.06.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading He-W 500); ss by #5742, eff 12-1-93, EXPIRED: 12-1-99\n\nNew. #7392, eff 10-28-00; ss by #7680, eff 4-20-02; ss by #7712, INTERIM, eff 6-22-02, EXPIRED: 12-19-02\n\nNew. #7805, eff 12-21-02; ss by #9831, eff 12-21-10; ss by #12529, eff 5-22-18",
